<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- The BAP 8th Cir. brief's Word styles; fb render builds docx/reference.docx from pandoc's default reference with
     them (tools/fb/src/docxref.rs). They are the styles of the cross-engine layout model (lib/docx/xengine-reference.sh
     font="Times New Roman" size=28 body=644 single=322 indent=720 heading=368 quote=280 note_after=140 footer=720;
     docs/EVAL-LOOP.md, "Cross-engine gate"), matching typst/bap8-opening-brief.typ: Times New Roman 14 pt
     (FRBP 8015(a)(5)(A)), Body Text in 32.2 pt line boxes with a half-inch first-line indent (double spacing,
     FRBP 8015(a)(4); typst line-pitch), quotations and footnotes 14 pt in 16.1 pt boxes (typst pitch-single), exact
     line spacing, widow control, 1 in margins on US Letter; plus the paragraph styles front.jq and brief.lua write the
     cover, front matter, headings, tables and certificates in, with the typst template's pitches and spaces
     (twips = 20 x pt): contents rows wrap before the 36 pt page column (typst toc-page-col), authorities before the
     56 pt one (toa-page-col; brief.lua widens it for a longer list), a dot leader to a right tab at the 6.5 in text
     width. The footer (a centered PAGE field) carries the id rIdBapFooter the front matter's sections name; the body
     section numbers its pages from 1. -->
